        unescoIntangible=['Kushtdepdi rite of singing and dancing', 'Traditional Turkmen carpet making art in Turkmenistan', 'Dutar making craftsmanship and traditional music performing art combined with singing', 'Art of Akhal-Teke horse breeding and traditions of horse decoration (inscribed 2023)'],
        famousPeople=['Magtymguly Pyragy', 'Alp Arslan', 'Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow', 'Serdar Berdimuhamedow', 'Polina Guryeva (Olympic medalist)', 'Saparmurat Niyazov', 'Kurban Berdyev (renowned football manager)'],
        flagDescription='A green field (symbolizing nature and Islam) featuring a vertical red stripe near the hoist containing five traditional carpet guls (tribal carpet medallions representing Teke, Yomut, Saryk, Chowdur, and Ersari) stacked vertically above two crossed olive branches (symbolizing permanent neutrality); to the right of the stripe in the upper canton is a white waxing crescent moon and five white five-pointed stars (representing the five provinces of Turkmenistan) (most complex flag design in the world).',
        coatOfArmsDescription='An eight-pointed green star (Rub El Hizb) with gold borders, containing a blue circle depicting a lifelike portrait of the legendary Akhal-Teke stallion Yanardag, enclosed by five carpet guls, sheaves of wheat, cotton bolls, and a crescent moon with five stars.',
        symbols={'animal': 'Akhal-Teke horse ("Heavenly Horse" - famed for metallic golden sheen and endurance) and Central Asian shepherd dog (Alabay)', 'bird': 'Lanner falcon', 'tree': 'Turkmen juniper (Arça)', 'flower': 'Wild desert tulip'},
        landmarks=['Darvaza Gas Crater ("The Door to Hell" - flaming crater in the Karakum Desert)', 'Ashgabat White Marble Cityscape and Alem Cultural Center', 'Ancient Merv (Mausoleum of Sultan Sanjar and Erk Gala)', 'Old Nisa Parthian Fortresses', 'Kunya-Urgench Minaret and Mausoleums', 'Kow Ata Underground Sulfur Thermal Lake', 'Kopet Dag Mountains and Health Path', 'Karakum Desert dunes', 'Arkadag Smart City'],
        travelNotes='Visas are mandatory for all foreign visitors; standard tourist entry requires an official Letter of Invitation (LOI) approved by the State Migration Service and booking through licensed local travel agencies; traveling to the Darvaza gas crater requires a 4WD vehicle and desert camping; photography is restricted around government buildings and presidential palaces in Ashgabat; mobile roaming is limited; cash (USD or Euro) is required as foreign credit cards have very limited acceptance outside luxury hotels.',
        shortSummary='Turkmenistan is an enigmatic, energy-rich Central Asian nation of permanent neutrality, famed for the blazing desert spectacle of the Darvaza Gas Crater ("The Door to Hell"), the gleaming white-marble architecture of Ashgabat, the peerless golden Akhal-Teke horses, and ancient Silk Road ruins at Merv.'
